    "create_time": 1773020967.148,
    "update_time": null,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Most likely nothing additional is taxable from the 1098-T, since scholarships equal qualified tuition, and you can't take an education credit on those expenses. Your taxable income is the W-2 stipend. Keep the 1098-T with your records."
     ]
    },
